From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:23:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: text-input: show and hide the input panel only for the focused client
Description:
 show_input_panel and hide_input_panel were honoured from any client.
 A client without text input focus, e.g. an application in the
 background that moves focus to one of its text fields, could open the
 on-screen keyboard over the active window or close it while the user
 was typing there.
 .
 Ignore these requests unless the client owns the surface that has text
 input focus, for text-input-v2 and text-input-v3.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL and GPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
---
